**No, you no longer need `TestingPlatformDotnetTestSupport` on .NET 10.** That property is only required for .NET 9 and earlier SDKs.

On .NET 10, add a `"test"` section to `global.json` instead:

```json
{
  "sdk": {
    "version": "10.0.100"
  },
  "test": {
    "runner": "Microsoft.Testing.Platform"
  }
}
```

This enables native MTP mode in `dotnet test` — arguments are passed directly (no `--` separator needed).

Want me to update your `global.json` and remove the now-unnecessary `TestingPlatformDotnetTestSupport` property from your `.csproj`?
